  "articleBody": "One of the big questions we get about natural stone tile is whether it needs sealing. And the short answer? Most of the time, yes! Many natural stones are porous, meaning they have tiny little holes that can absorb liquids and stains. To protect your beautiful investment and keep it looking great for years, sealing is a must. You'll want to seal it right after installation, and then, depending on the type of stone and how much traffic it gets, you'll typically need to reseal it every 1–2 years. Think of it like putting sunscreen on your skin – it protects it from damage. Sealing acts as a barrier, making your stone much more resistant to spills and grime. Skipping this step can lead to permanent discoloration or staining, which nobody wants. If you're working with a professional, they'll make sure this crucial step is covered for you. It's a simple process that makes a huge difference in the longevity and appearance of your natural stone.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}